<p><span><strong>Testing Tools &amp; Tips!</strong></span></p>
<p>You will have these buttons to help you on the test. I strongly recomend using 5 then 7 and coming back to questions later using 2.</p>
<p><span><strong><img style="display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;" src="https://github.com/dsquireazva/foundations-of-digital-literacy/blob/main/Level%201%20Exam/Attempt1-001.png?raw=true" data-api-returntype="File" /></strong></span></p>
<p>1. Resets the question you are currently on. Great to do this if your question glitches and you can&rsquo;t move on</p>
<p>2. Question List &ndash; You can use this to navigate through the test questions quickly (use this with the &ldquo;Mark for Review&rdquo; button)</p>
<p>3. Tt &ndash; Allows you to make the text of the instructions bigger</p>
<p>4. Clock &ndash; Shows you how much time you have left</p>
<p>5. Mark &hellip; - Mark for Review Button. If you are struggling to do this question, click this button to review it later. The more questions you get through quickly, the more time you have left to work on the hard ones.</p>
<p>6. Skip &ndash; skip this question and move on to the next. Marks it as complete even if you do not complete it.</p>
<p>7. Next &ndash; go to the next question. Does not mark it as complete or for review.</p>
<p><span style="background-color: #fbeeb8;">If you pass both attempts with 80% or higher, you will be eligible to take the Official Certification Exam. Your teacher will reach out to help you with this.&nbsp;</span></p>
